Plan: Cast Cycle of Renewal to ramp. Sacrifice a Forest, get two tapped Forests. That leaves me with... I have 3 untapped Forests. Cycle costs {2}{G} = 3 mana. I'd tap all 3 Forests, sacrifice one, then get 2 tapped basics. So my board would be: 2 tapped new Forests + Food + Leaves saga. Next turn I'd have 4 Forests, allowing 4-mana plays.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, cast Leaves from the Vine now ({1}{G}) and keep mana? But then I only have 2 mana left, can't cast Cycle. Casting Cycle now is better for ramp.\n\
\n\
Graveyard: Cycle of Renewal, Forest, Mountain (milled by Leaves chapter I presumably). Interesting — there's a Mountain in graveyard. Cycle of Renewal searches for basic lands — if I have Mountains in deck, fetching a Mountain would enable... nothing red in hand currently. Earth Rumble Wrestlers is hybrid {3}{R/G} so castable with green. So just fetch Forests, unless I want a Mountain for something. No need.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — Earthbend Lesson targets a land, makes it a 4/4 haste creature. With Leaves chapter III coming next turn (draw if creature or Lesson card in graveyard — Lesson is a card type; Earthbending Lesson is presumably a Lesson? It says \"Earthbend 4\" — the Lesson subtype might be on it. Actually in Avatar set, \"Lesson\" is a subtype. Leaves III draws if creature or Lesson card in graveyard. Currently graveyard has Cycle of Renewal, Forest, Mountain — no creature or Lesson. Milling happens at chapter I only. So next turn chapter III: draw only if I have a creature/Lesson in graveyard by then. Casting Earthbending Lesson puts a Lesson in graveyard after resolution — enabling the draw if I cast it before the saga triggers? The saga trigger happens after my draw step, so I'd need a Lesson/creature in gy already at that point. Hmm, chapter III triggers after draw step at the beginning of precombat main. If I cast Earthbending Lesson this turn... but I can't afford both Cycle (3) and Lesson (4) with 3 mana.\n\
\n\
Sequence: This turn (T3 postcombat): cast Cycle of Renewal, sacrifice Forest, fetch 2 tapped Forests. Board: 4 Forests total (2 tapped + ... wait. I have 3 Forests. Tap all 3 to pay {2}{G}. Sacrifice one as additional cost. Fetch 2 basics tapped. Net: I had 3 forests, sacrificed 1, gained 2 = 4 Forests, all tapped. Next turn: 4 mana untapped + saga chapter III.\n\
\n\
Next turn options with 4 mana: Earthbending Lesson (earthbend 4 — a 4/4 haste land) or Earth Rumble Wrestlers (3/4 reach, +1/+0 trample since a land entered this turn) or Vinebender (4/3). Earthbending Lesson makes a 4/4 haste — immediate attacker. Also puts Lesson in gy, but chapter III trigger already happened by then... Actually, if I cast the Lesson BEFORE... no, saga lore counter is added after draw step, trigger goes on stack. I could respond? No, casting Lesson in response to the trigger wouldn't help since trigger checks on resolution — actually it checks \"if there's a creature or Lesson card in your graveyard\" at resolution! So I could cast Earthbending Lesson with the chapter III trigger on the stack, then the Lesson resolves first (goes to gy as Lesson card... wait, Lesson is a subtype — Earthbending Lesson is likely \"Sorcery — Lesson\". After it resolves it goes to graveyard. Then chapter III trigger resolves and sees a Lesson in gy → draw a card!\n\
\n\
So next turn: draw step, chapter III trigger on stack, cast Earthbending Lesson (4 mana available), it resolves, then trigger sees Lesson in gy → draw. And I get a 4/4 haste land creature that can attack.\n\
\n\
Alternatively Vinebender or Wrestlers next turn. Earthbending Lesson gives haste 4/4 attacker + draw. \n\
\n\
This turn: definitely Cycle of Renewal. Sacrifice a Forest, fetch 2 Forests (or 1 Forest + 1 Mountain for flexibility). Earth Rumble Wrestlers is hybrid so no need for Mountain. Fetch 2 Forests.\n\
\n\
One consideration: should I play the second Leaves from the Vine instead? {1}{G} — leaves 2 mana unused. Two sagas could be nice but ramping first is better for the 4-drops. Also, chapter II needs creatures to put counters on — currently none. Next turn I'll hopefully have an earthbent land as a creature for future counters.\n\
\n\
Note: The earthbent land (with counters) is a creature — Leaves chapter II could put counters on it. Good synergy.\n\
\n\
