Opponent's board: Earthbender Ascension with landfall quest counters, Tolls of War (sacrifice → 1/1 Ally), Kyoshi Village 2/2, Clue token. They're tapped out, so no instant-speed interaction this turn (unless they have 0-mana stuff, unlikely).\n\
\n\
Attack math: My 4/4 haste vs their 2/2 Village. If they block with Village, Village dies, my 4/4 takes 2, survives as 4/2. They lose their Village permanently (it's a land creature but when it dies... Kyoshi Village doesn't have the earthbend return clause — it entered as a creature-land? Wait, how is Kyoshi Village a 2/2? It says \"Kyoshi Village 2/2: enters tapped, {T}: Add {G}, {T}: Add {W}, {4}{T} Sac: draw, Haste\". Hmm, it seems Kyoshi Village is inherently a creature? It's a land creature — a 2/2 with haste? It has 2 +1/+1 counters \"included in 2/2\". So it's a 0/0? No wait — \"Kyoshi Village 2/2 (tapped, 2 +1/+1 counters, included in 2/2)\". So base 0/0 + 2 counters = 2/2? That suggests it was earthbent by the opponent (Earthbender Ascension earthbends 2: 0/0 + 2 counters). Yes! Opponent's Ascension entered, earthbend 2 on Kyoshi Village → 2/2 haste. So if it dies, it returns to the battlefield tapped (as a land). So blocking isn't as costly for them — the Village returns tapped.\n\
\n\
So if they block: my 4/4 deals 4 to their 2/2, it dies and returns tapped; my land takes 2 damage, survives. They prevent 4 damage but lose... nothing much, Village returns tapped. Hmm. So they might block. Still, trading their blocker for no damage taken is fine for me either way — I develop a 4/4.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, is there a better play? What about Vinebender (4/3, can't be blocked by power 2 or less)? No haste. Next turn attack. The Lesson line is faster.\n\
\n\
Let me also think: do I want to attack with the earthbent land into their board? They have only the 2/2 Village as a potential blocker. Yes, attack.\n\
\n\
Alright: cast Earthbending Lesson. I'll use auto-tap. Then target the untapped land.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me get the game state first to see IDs so I can control the mana plan precisely and know which land to target. Actually the targeting prompt will come after I choose to cast. Let me just cast now with choice=\"p5\".\n\
\n\
One more consideration: should I play Leaves from the Vine first (2 mana), then... no, then I'd only have 3 mana, can't cast Lesson (4). No.\n\
\n\
Could I cast both Leaves and a 4-drop? 2+4=6 > 5. No. So Lesson alone, 1 mana wasted. That's fine.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — should I consider not casting Lesson and instead casting Wrestlers + saving? No, Lesson is best.\n\
\n\
Also Food token activation — no.\n\
\n\
Let me cast Earthbending Lesson[p5].",
