Let me also think: is there a line where I kill Hei Bai for sure? Soldier pump → 5/5 attack. They choose whether Hei Bai trades. If they value Hei Bai, they take 5. Either way I win something.\n\
\n\
What about the danger of a pump spell saving Hei Bai when it blocks? They have B mana only. Possible but the trade still mostly happens (my land returns).\n\
\n\
I'll go with the Soldier line as planned in my summary. Actually hold on, let me reconsider Badgermole once more...\n\
\n\
The case for Badgermole: my deck is an earthbend synergy deck. Badgermole + Bitter Work exhaust (4 mana earthbend 4) next turn: attack with 4/4 trample Mountain, 2/2 trample land, 4/4 Badgermole... but opponent untaps and develops too. Their Hei Bai becomes a must-answer threat. Without Soldier's pump, my Mountain stays 4/4 — Hei Bai eats it in combat (well, it returns).\n\
\n\
The case for Soldier: immediate 5/5 trample-less attacker forces the issue now. Also vigilance lets it block.\n\
\n\
One more idea: cast Soldier, pump Mountain to 5/5, attack. If they block with Hei Bai → trade (great). If they take 5 → 7 life, then next turn Badgermole + attack with 5/5 (trample!) + 2/2 haste land... they take trample damage or chump. Seems strong.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait. Let me reconsider whether to attack at all vs. holding back for blocks. They're at 12 with a big board; I'm at 16. If I don't attack, they untap and swing with Hei Bai (7/7 after sac) + Trebuchet token + Allies. I'd take ~8-10. Then I'm at ~6-8. Too dangerous. I need to pressure and force them to use resources.\n\
\n\
Attack plan it is. Cast Earth Kingdom Soldier now.\n\
\n\
Mana: 4 Forests (p7, p8, p46, p49) + Mountain p56 = {4}{G} — Soldier costs {4}{G/W}, pay G/W with G. Fine.\n\
\n\
Then ETB trigger: put +1/+1 counter on up to two target creatures I control → Mountain p57 (→5/5) and Soldier itself (→4/5).\n\
\n\
Then attack with the 5/5 Mountain.\n\
\n\
Wait — should the Soldier get the counter or should I pump only the Mountain? \"up to two target creatures\" — targeting Soldier itself makes it 4/5 vigilance, which is better for blocking Hei Bai next turn (still dies to 5/5... but if Hei Bai is 7/7, everything dies anyway). Yes, pump Soldier too.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually one question: does the counter on the Mountain make it a 5/5 and Bitter Work still triggers? Yes, power 5 ≥ 4.\n\
\n\
Also: after casting Soldier, all my lands except the 5/5 Mountain are tapped. The 5/5 attacks, taps. Then I'm fully tapped out — fine, it's my turn.\n\
\n\
Let me also consider sequence: cast Soldier first, then attack. Yes.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me double-check the alternative of Badgermole one final time... You know, there's a hybrid: what if I cast Badgermole, earthbend 2 targeting Mountain p56 (the untapped one I'm not attacking with)... then attack with 4/4 trample Mountain p57 + 2/2 trample Mountain p56. Same as before. Hei Bai blocks 4/4, Trebuchet blocks 2/2 (or Hei Bai blocks 2/2 and Trebuchet blocks 4/4 → Trebuchet dies!). Opponent chooses: likely Hei Bai on 4/4 (kills it, takes 4, survives), Trebuchet on 2/2 (takes 2, survives). Nothing gained except Bitter Work card.\n\
\n\
vs Soldier: 5/5 attack, Hei Bai trades or they take 5.\n\
\n\
Soldier line is better this turn. Go.\n\
\n\
Actually, hmm, wait. Let me reconsider: in the Soldier line, if they take 5 (12→7), they keep Hei Bai. Next turn they untap, play a land (Ascension trigger: +1/+1 and trample on something), attack with Hei Bai 7/7 trample-ish + 2/1 flyer + 2/2 Ally + maybe 1/1. That's ~11 damage in the air... I'd block Hei Bai with Soldier (4/5) — Hei Bai survives, I take... trample? If Ascension gives Hei Bai trample and it's 7/7 blocked by 4/5: 4 to Soldier... wait, 7 damage: assign lethal (5) to Soldier, 2 trample through. Plus 2/1 flyer + 2/2 Ally unblocked if my 5/5 Mountain... I'd block flyer with the Mountain? Mountain is a 5/5 — blocks 2/1 flyer, kills it, survives. Take 2 from Ally + 2 trample = 4. I'm at 12. Then my turn: attack with 5/5 + 4/5... wait Soldier died. Attack with 5/5 Mountain (trample if I cast Badgermole). They're at 7. If they have Hei Bai 7/7 back... this gets grindy.\n\
\n\
Alternatively if they trade Hei Bai for my land this turn: their board is Trebuchet, 2/2 Ally, 1/1 Ally, Ascension, Tolls. Much more manageable. My 5/5... wait, the Mountain returns tapped as a land (no counters? Let me check earthbend rules: \"When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped.\" Does it return with counters? Typically earthbend returns the land card — the counters... The rule text says \"return it to the battlefield tapped\" — it returns as a land, and the +1/+1 counters... hmm, in the actual Avatar set, earthbend returns the land with its counters? Let me recall: Earthbend mechanic: \"Target land you control becomes a 0/0 creature with haste that's still a land. Put N +1/+1 counters on it. When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped.\" When it returns, it's a new object — a land, not a creature, no counters. I believe the counters don't persist (new object). So the Mountain returns as a plain tapped Mountain. The Soldier's +1/+1 counter on it would also be lost. Fine — lands are resilient, that's the point.\n\
\n\
OK, decision made: Cast Earth Kingdom Soldier, target Mountain p57 and itself with counters, attack with the 5/5.\n\
\n\
Actually, hold on. Let me reconsider one more time whether to pump the Soldier itself or maybe not attack and set up a double-block... No. Pressure is right. They're at 12; every point matters, and trading a returning land for Hei Bai is excellent.\n\
\n\
Let me also chat a bit — I should engage. The last few turns had no chat mentioned. I'll send a quick message.\n\
\n\
First action: cast Earth Kingdom Soldier (p43). Mana plan: tap p7, p8, p46, p49 (Forests) + p56 (Mountain). Auto-tap should handle it. I'll let auto-tap work but maybe specify to avoid tapping the 4/4 Mountain p57! Auto-tap might tap p57 for R... The Soldier cost is {4}{G/W} — auto-tap should prefer basic... risky. Better to specify mana_plan explicitly: \"p7,p8,p46,p49,p56\". That gives GGGG + R = 5 mana, paying 4 generic with 3G+1R andG with the last G. Good.\n\
\n\
Let me do it.",
