      "thinking": "Let me look at the situation. Earth Kingdom Soldier's ETB trigger is on the stack. I need to select up to two target creatures I control to put +1/+1 counters on.\n\
\n\
My creatures: Earth Kingdom Soldier (3/4, sick) and Mountain 4/4 (with 4 counters, can attack since it's a land creature with haste from earthbend).\n\
\n\
Plan: put both counters... wait, the trigger says \"put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures you control.\" So I select two creatures, each gets one counter. I should target both the Soldier and the Mountain. That makes Mountain a 5/5 and Soldier a 4/5.\n\
\n\
The choice interface says \"Select creatures you control (selected 0 of 2)\". Choices: Earth Kingdom Soldier [p43], Mountain [p57]. I need to select both. Let me choose p43 first, then p57. Actually the respond format is choice=pN — I probably need to select one at a time. Let me select Mountain first (p57), then Soldier (p43).\n\
\n\
Actually, can I select the same creature twice? The trigger says \"up to two target creatures\" — each target must be a different creature typically. So one counter each on Soldier and Mountain.\n\
\n\
Mountain becomes 5/5 (well, 0/0 + 5 counters = 5/5).Soldier becomes 4/5.\n\
\n\
Let me select p57 (Mountain) first.",
