      "thinking": "The Soldier's ETB trigger is on the stack, targeting Mountain first. I selected 1 of 2 targets. Now I need to select the second target — the Soldier itself (p43). That gives the Soldier a counter, making it a 4/5 vigilance.\n\
\n\
Wait, let me think. The Mountain 4/4 becomes 5/5. The Soldier becomes 4/5. Both would have counters, which matters for Badgermole's trample later.\n\
\n\
Actually, should I put the second counter on the Mountain to make it a 6/6 instead? Options: Mountain (5/5) + Soldier (4/5), or Mountain (6/6) alone.\n\
\n\
With Bitter Work, attacking with a 4+ power creature draws a card. A 5/5 Mountain already qualifies. Making the Soldier a 4/5 gives it a counter for Badgermole trample synergy and makes it a bigger vigilance blocker/attacker. The Soldier is summoning sick this turn anyway.\n\
\n\
Opponent has Hei Bai 5/5 (with 2 counters, so it's actually 5/5 base 3/3? No — Hei Bai is 5/5 with 2 +1/+1 counters included... wait it says \"Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance 5/5 (sick, 2 +1/+1 counters, included in 5/5)\". So Hei Bai is normally 3/3, and with 2 counters it's 5/5).\n\
\n\
Next turn I play Badgermole (4/4, earthbend 2, gives trample to creatures with counters). The Soldier with a counter would have trample. So putting the second counter on the Soldier is good.\n\
\n\
Selectp43 (Earth Kingdom Soldier) as the second target.",
