Actually, hmm, wait. Let me reconsider. Am I sure the opponent will all-out attack? They're at 12 life. If they tap out attacking and I survive with a board, they might fear my counterattack. But with Hei Bai at 9/9 surviving (it blocks... no it's attacking). After their all-in, their board: Hei Bai tapped, Drill tapped, everything tapped. My turn 8: if I have lethal... In Option 1: my creatures all died. I have 7 mana, hand: Wrestlers, Vinebender, Leaves, Moose-Lion. Cast Moose-Lion (7/7), attack? 7/7 vs their tapped board — no blockers untapped except... everything's tapped! Attack for 7 → opp at 5. Then turn 9 they untap and kill me (I'm at 3). They'd have Hei Bai 9/9 + Drill + 10/10... wait no, in Option 1 non-Ascension line: Hei Bai survived at 9/9 (took 6, damage clears at cleanup). Their turn 9: Hei Bai attacks, sacs → 11/11, Drill crews, allies... I have Moose-Lion 7/7 + maybe Vinebender/Wrestlers (turn 8: 7 mana — Moose-Lion 6, or Wrestlers 4 + Vinebender 4 = 8 no; Wrestlers + Leaves? ). Blockers: 7/7, maybe 4/4. vs 11/11 + 5/5 trample + 1/1s. Dead.\n\
