Blocks: I must block both big ones? 4/4 blocks Hei Bai (dies to 9/9... wait, Badgermole 4/4 vs 9/9: Badgermole deals 4 to Hei Bai, Hei Bai deals 9 to Badgermole. Badgermole dies, Hei Bai survives at 9/5 effectively). 2/2 blocks Drill: 7 trample - 2 = 5 through. Unblocked Allies: 2+1+1+1 = 5. Total: 10. Dead.\n\
\n\
Block Drill with 4/4: 7-4 = 3 trample through. Block Hei Bai with 2/2: Hei Bai has no trample, all 9 absorbed, 2/2 dies (returns tapped as land). Unblocked Allies: 5. Total: 3+5 = 8. Dead.\n\
\n\
Hmm. Either way I die unless they don't attack with everything or I gain life. Can I gain life? Food needs 2 mana. I have 1 untapped land. No.\n\
\n\
Wait — actually, maybe I should reconsider. Is there any way to get more blockers? What if I earthbend a tapped land instead, and keep p52 untapped for... nothing useful. No.\n\
\n\
What about blocking with the 5/5 Mountain? It's tapped from attacking; it stays tapped through their turn. No.\n\
\n\
Hmm, what about the Food token — it costs {2}, tap, sacrifice. I have 1 mana. No.\n\
\n\
So I'm likely dead on board to a full alpha strike. But wait — let me recount their attackers. Hei Bai 7/7 → 9/9 with sacrifice. Drill 7/7. Ally 2/2, Ally 1/1, Ally 1/1 (sick now, will be fine next turn). Plus Tolls trigger gives another 1/1 when they sacrifice for Hei Bai. That's 9+7+2+1+1+1 = 21 vs my 4 life and blockers 4/4 + 2/2 (and the 2/2 is a land that returns).\n\
\n\
Optimal block: block Hei Bai with Badgermole (no trample, absorb all 9), block Drill with 2/2 (absorb 2, 5 trample), Allies get through for 5. Total 10. Dead.\n\
\n\
Block Hei Bai with 2/2 (absorb 9, land returns), block Drill with 4/4 (absorb 4, 3 trample), Allies 5. Total 8. Dead.\n\
\n\
Double-block Hei Bai with both: absorb 9, both die... Hei Bai trample? No. Both blockers die (4/4 kills nothing, 9/9 kills both; actually Badgermole deals 4 to Hei Bai, 2/2 deals 2 → 6 total, Hei Bai 9 toughness survives). Then Drill 7 trample + Allies 5 = 12 unblocked. Dead.\n\
\n\
So unless opponent misplays or doesn't have the sacrifice... they have tokens to sacrifice for sure. I might just be dead. But maybe they won't attack optimally, or maybe they don't crew Drill to keep blockers? They're at 12; my board: 5/5 Mountain (tapped, untaps next turn), Badgermole 4/4, 2/2 land. If they alpha strike and I somehow survive... \n\
\n\
Actually wait — maybe I should think about whether to crack Food... I can't (only 1 mana).\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually, one more consideration: should I have NOT attacked with the Mountain to keep it as a blocker? Too late — already attacked and it killed the Trebuchet and drew a card. That was the recap's decision; can't change.\n\
\n\
OK so the play now: earthbend the untapped Forest p52 (the only untapped land) so the 2/2 can block. Wait, actually, let me reconsider whether to earthbend a tapped land vs untapped:\n\
\n\
- Earthbend untapped p52: creature is untapped 2/2, can block. ✓\n\
- Earthbend tapped land: creature is tapped, cannot block. ✗\n\
\n\
Definitely p52.\n\
\n\
Also note: p52 as a creature can still tap for mana. If I need mana on their turn... no instant-speed uses in hand. Fine.\n\
\n\
After choosing the target, Badgermole ETB resolves, then I'm in postcombat main with 1 untapped land-creature (2/2). Nothing to cast (cheapest spell is Leaves {1}{G} — wait, Leaves from the Vine costs {1}{G} = 2 mana. I have 1. Earth Rumble Wrestlers {3}{R/G} = 4. Vinebender {3}{G} = 4. Moose-Lion {4}{G}{G} = 6. Forestcycling {2} = 2 mana to cycle Moose-Lion for a Forest. Can't afford any.\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, actually — should I have NOT played the Forest this turn and instead... no, the recap says I played Forest to hit 7 mana for Badgermole + Food activation. Badgermole costs {3}{G}... wait, what's Badgermole's cost? Not shown, but from recap \"Badgermole (4/4 that earthbends 2...)\" — I had 7 lands, played Forest → 7 lands? Let me count my lands: p7, p8, p46, p49, p52 Forests (5), p56, p57 Mountains (2) = 7 lands. Badgermole presumably costs {3}{G}{G} = 5? Then I'd have 2 left for Food... but all lands are tapped except p52. So 1 left. Hmm, maybe Badgermole costs {4}{G} = 5, or {3}{G}{G}. Either way I have 1 mana left, not 2. So no Food activation.\n\
\n\
OK. Choose p52 for the earthbend target.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait. Let me reconsider: maybe picking the untapped Forest is wrong because I want to use that mana for... nothing. Everything costs 2+. The blocker is worth more. Yes, p52.\n\
\n\
One more thought: could I earthbend the 5/5 Mountain p57 to add 2 more counters making it 7/7? It's tapped (attacked), so it can't block anyway. Adding counters doesn't help defense. No.\n\
\n\
