      "reasoning": "Looking at the combat math: I'm at 4 life facing three attackers — Ally 2/2, Hei Bai 10/10 with trample, and the Drill 6/3 with trample. I have two blockers (Badgermole 4/4, Forest 2/2) totaling 6 toughness against 18 power, and both big attackers trample. No matter how I assign blocks, exactly 12 damage gets through (18 − 6 absorbed), and my Food token costs {2} with only 1 untapped land. There's no line that survives — I'll make the blocks that at least take the Drill down with me and say good game.",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze this carefully. I'm at 4 life. Incoming attackers:\n\
- Ally Token 2/2 (p109)\n\
- Hei Bai 10/10 (p66) — has trample? The card reference says \"Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance 10/10: ... / Trample\" — yes, it gained trample from Earthbender Ascension's landfall trigger (when quest counters 4+, target creature gets +1/+1 counter and gains trample until end of turn). Actually wait, the trample listed is likely from Ascension's trigger.\n\
- The Fire Nation Drill 6/3 (p15) — trample, crewed.\n\
\n\
My blockers: Forest 2/2 (p52, land creature with 2 counters) and Badgermole 4/4 (p38, summoning sick but can block).\n\
\n\
Total incoming: 2 + 10 + 6 = 18 damage. I'm at 4 life. If I don't block everything, I die.\n\
\n\
